														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-1793581">
									

<p>I want to upvote it, but&#8230;</p>
<p>This is inconsistent! From the description:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Following the encounter, SCP-1395-A will demanifest, erasing all memories of the encounter from the individual(s)' mind.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>If that's the case, then how is it that</p>
<blockquote>
<p>SCP-1395 was discovered in 19██ after reports of a &quot;ghost cave&quot; reached the Greek government.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>If no one can remember their encounters with the shade, how could the Greek government have known about it? How could the Foundation have decided it was important to continue investigating it? It doesn't make any sense, and not in the good way.</p>
<p>I'm down-voting for the present. If you can fix this error and make it convincing within 24 hrs, I'm sure that will be enough to turn my vote around.</p>
<p>E: I've rescinded my -1 since this was first posted, but without actually incorporating the justification into the SCiP, it does not yet warrant a +1.</p>

							</div>

								
